  "id": "DrugBank_DB11077 - MONDO_948",
  "verbalization": "Polyethylene Glycol 400 is associated with Xerophthalmia through a chain of off-label use and indications. The drug is known to cause Dry Eye Syndrome, which in turn is linked to Xerophthalmia via its indications on Propylene Glycol and Polyvinyl Alcohol. These substances, though not directly linked to Xerophthalmia in standard clinical settings, may contribute to the condition through their effects on ocular surface hydration and inflammation. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where the off-label use of Polyethylene Glycol 400 could indirectly lead to Xerophthalmia by exacerbating dry eye symptoms, which are a known precursor to the condition. The overlapping pathways highlight a possible role of these compounds in ocular health, though the exact mechanism remains unclear and requires further investigation.",
